From f0a5488a121140ad37b022b43bafe5ed7896032a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+, the first picture
 of a scene waits for its measurement where it can

The first picture of a scene (the module said so when the renderer asked for
its InfoFrame, before it was drawn) waits, once it is drawn and its samples
are queued, for its own measurement, until 4 ms before the next vblank
(dvbridge_dvplus_wait_budget(): the vblank of the output read with the
vblank ioctl, the period of the mode). Measured in time, it goes out with
its scene's own metadata (SetHDR10Plus() again for that frame, and when it is
shown again); not in time, with the metadata of the scene before, as before.
Where the vblanks cannot be read (nvidia-drm with its defaults), it does not
wait, and kodi.log says so once.

The help of the setting says it (core 40927, Estuary 32101 in en_gb, es_es,
es_ar and es_mx). kodi.log, in the line of every 240 frames: how many first pictures went out
with their own measurement, how many were not measured by the vblank, and how
many had no vblank to wait by.

What the wait costs on a graphics chip is the time from the end of the
frame's GPU work to its commit (the samples read, the statistics, the
InfoFrame: about 0.6 ms on the build machine), and whether it comes in time
depends on how long that GPU work is: not measured on hardware.
