-msgid "For a display that takes HDR10+ and not Dolby Vision, as many Samsung TVs. A Dolby Vision video rebuilt as HDR10 is sent as HDR10+: with each scene, dynamic metadata that Hades measures from the rebuilt picture (the average and the distribution of its brightness), so that the display adapts each scene as it adapts an HDR10+ film. The scenes are those of the Dolby Vision metadata. These metadata are not the studio's, and no tone curve is sent: the display makes its own. Profile 8.1 is then rebuilt too; profile 7 as the setting above says. The first picture of a scene goes out with the metadata of the scene before (the picture is measured after it is drawn), and the display may show a scene otherwise than as plain HDR10. Not while the picture is mapped to the display. Applies from the next video."
